WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.425
So, four decisions.

2
00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:05.014
Put the identity-verification
procedure under the CISO,

3
00:00:05.014 --> 00:00:08.752
and treat every authenticator
reset as an account transfer:

4
00:00:08.752 --> 00:00:13.462
the most friction on the most sensitive
accounts, and an alert on every reset.

5
00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:14.850
Build one front door.

6
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.019
Redirect the team mailbox,
triage by authority,

7
00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:21.188
and let unanswered
approvals expire to reject.

8
00:00:21.188 --> 00:00:24.588
Buy the platform's native
compliance applications first,

9
00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:26.288
and build only what they lack.

10
00:00:26.288 --> 00:00:30.941
Record an authorization verdict before
any SaaS integration is configured,

11
00:00:30.941 --> 00:00:33.413
and check every feature in your own cloud.

12
00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:36.253
And fund the third
layer: an owner, a gate,

13
00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:39.626
a clock and an evidence
feed for every control.

14
00:00:39.626 --> 00:00:41.825
The next step needs no procurement.

15
00:00:41.825 --> 00:00:46.741
Measure before you build: run the
read-only integration inventory and

16
00:00:46.741 --> 00:00:52.081
synchronization probe in a test tenant,
size the catalog from what they find,

17
00:00:52.081 --> 00:00:56.913
and plan the move off AWS's ServiceNow
connector before March 31, 2027.

18
00:00:56.913 --> 00:01:01.613
Operations is where modernization
becomes routine or quietly reverts.

19
00:01:01.613 --> 00:01:05.337
Book 15 has the detail,
every claim footnoted.

20
00:01:05.337 --> 00:01:06.170
Thank you.
